{
  "_comment": [
    "The first dream-audience: the dead god, to the one who killed it.",
    "",
    "Every node is INITIATOR, and that is the design rather than laziness. Every other",
    "scene in the mod is an ensemble where each player has an equal voice -- that is",
    "what redeems the pseudo-main-character. This is the ONE table nobody else sits at,",
    "and the contrast is the point. The asymmetry is a room, not a privilege.",
    "",
    "The ghost calls them EXECUTOR and never explains it, because an executor is the",
    "person who settles an estate. The word is doing the work; a line explaining it",
    "would take the work away. Never state the theme.",
    "",
    "Dread covenant: the grief is sincere throughout and is never the punchline. What",
    "is allowed to be funny is the god's pettiness about small things and the sheer",
    "administrative shape of what it wants -- it is not seeking revenge, it is trying",
    "to hand over a job.",
    "",
    "NOTE: the god says 'a family' and never a number. The pantheon roster is still",
    "[WORKSHOP] in WORLD.md, and shipped dialogue that counted them would settle a",
    "question the owner has not settled."
  ],
